<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cuban Missile Crisis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as October Crisis, Caribbean Crisis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cuban Missile Crisis of October 1962 was the closest the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> came to nuclear war. After American reconnaissance flights found Soviet nuclear missile sites under construction in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, President Kennedy imposed a naval quarantine of the island. After thirteen days of confrontation Khrushchev agreed to remove the missiles in return for an American pledge not to invade Cuba and the secret withdrawal of US missiles from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cuban-missile-crisis.jpg" alt="Cuban Missile Crisis" width="320" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: USAF · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PGM-19A_Jupiter_missile-02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Front de libération du Québec carried out bombings and, in the <b>October Crisis</b> of 1970, kidnappings that led Pierre Trudeau to invoke the War Measures Act, and the Parti Québécois held referendums on sovereignty in 1980, defeated by about 60 to 40 per cent, and in 1995,…</blockquote><a href="/empire/canada">Canada · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>The Soviet Union supported revolutionary and anti-colonial movements in China, Korea, Vietnam, Cuba, Angola and elsewhere, and the rivalry with the United States shaped international politics for over four decades, including the <b>Cuban Missile Crisis</b> of 1962.</blockquote><a href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…reworking on a version by Martí and Julián Orbón, as performed by Héctor Angulo, and meant it for the peace movement at the time of the <b>Cuban Missile Crisis</b>: he urged people to sing it, in Spanish, as a sign of unity between the American and Cuban peoples.</blockquote><a href="/songs/guantanamera">Guantanamera</a></li><li><blockquote>Signed in Geneva after the <b>Cuban Missile Crisis</b>, the agreement created a direct teletype link between Washington and Moscow.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-20">20 June in history</a></li></ul></section>
